ALTER TABLE contracts ADD COLUMN embedding_new vector(384);

-- backfill in batches from the application, then:
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY contracts_embedding_new_hnsw_idx
    ON contracts
    USING hnsw (embedding_new vector_cosine_ops);

BEGIN;
ALTER TABLE contracts DROP COLUMN embedding;
ALTER TABLE contracts RENAME COLUMN embedding_new TO embedding;
COMMIT;
```

A vector column's dimension is part of its type, so it cannot be widened in place -- you add, backfill, index concurrently, then swap. `CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY` avoids holding a write lock but cannot run inside a transaction block.

